summary: Discover tests relevant for execution

description: |
    Gather tests and their metadata for execution. Use the ``how`` key
    to select a discovery method, such as ``fmf`` for tests defined in
    an fmf tree or ``shell`` for tests defined directly in the plan.
    See the :ref:`/plugins/discover` documentation for available methods
    and supported options.

    The discover step stores the list of discovered tests together with
    their metadata in the ``tests.yaml`` file. The format is a list of
    dictionaries structured in the following way:

    .. code-block:: yaml

        - name: /test/one
          discover-phase: default-0
          summary: Short test summary.
          description: Long test description.
          contact: [Petr Šplíchal <psplicha@redhat.com>]
          component: [tmt]
          test: tmt --help
          path: /test/path/
          require: [package1, package2]
          environment:
              key1: value1
              key2: value2
              key3: value3
          duration: 5m
          enabled: true
          result: respect
          tag: [tag]
          tier: 1
          serial-number: 1

        - name: /test/two
          discover-phase: default-0
          summary: Short test summary.
          description: Long test description.
          ...

example: |
    discover:
        how: fmf
        filter: tier:1

link:
    - implemented-by: /tmt/steps/discover
